      "value": "@{6019bf5a7ae30b2338107fb4|full_name}: I'm sure that this is a legitimate OSC application. However, in addition to communicating with VRChat through OSC, it appears to also be using a function to check if VRChat is running. That function is not using OSC and while it is not \"modding\" the client in a way that would be against terms of service, it is still poking at VRChat in a way that triggers EAC. \nThis is something that we can bring up with Epic to see if they can allow. Alternatively, VRChat could implement some other method of informing applications that is running. We will have to investigate the options. In the meantime, applications should be changed to simply not worry about whether or not VRChat is running.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
