      "value": "@{60285ca04963ba22994f485b|full_name}: I suppose it depends on /how/ they're going about it exactly. I would assume that waiting on OSC to establish a connection would not violate ToS, but could still be used to make the same prompt. Likewise, there are methods to query the system directly rather than the client. Though those don't need to create an application hook to VRChat or its components, what you say seems to raise a gray area that needs to be clarified.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
