      "value": "@{6019bf5a7ae30b2338107fb4|full_name}: There are many different ways to tell if an application is open using various windows APIs. I do not know which ones trigger EAC and which ones do not. Unfortunately people will just have to experiment with that and see what works. However, none of those methods use OSC unless you choose to listen to port 9001, and only one application can do that at once so it is not ideal.\nWe understand that this is not a perfect solution as it is very handy to know when VRChat is running. There are several options that would solve this that we have already considered in the past, such as OSCQuery, but this issue will raise the priority of implementing those options.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
